{"id":"chatcmpl-4b79eebe-3b5b-44b8-895a-b6c71a193b9c","object":"chat.completion","created":1792457881,"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next-atlas","system_fingerprint":"fp_atlas","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"The user wants a clear, accessible explanation of how sourdough starter cultures work, written for a home baker. They specifically asked for \"plain paragraphs\" — so no bullet points, no numbered lists, no headers breaking things up into sections. Just flowing prose that a curious home baker could read and understand.\n\nI need to cover: what a starter actually is (the microbial community), how the fermentation works (wild yeast + lactic acid bacteria), what the feeding cycle does, why it rises and falls, the role of flour and water, and maybe a touch of why it's sour. I should keep the tone warm and practical, not textbook-dry. I'll avoid jargon where possible, or introduce it gently when it's useful.\n\nLet me write this as a few solid paragraphs that flow naturally from one idea to the next.\n","content":"A sourdough starter is a living community of microorganisms — mainly wild yeast and lactic acid bacteria — that you keep alive by feeding it flour and water on a regular schedule. Unlike commercial yeast, which is a single strain grown in a lab, a starter is a whole ecosystem. The yeast and bacteria come from the flour itself, from the air in your kitchen, and from your hands. Over time, the ones that thrive in your particular environment become dominant, which is why every starter is a little different and why bakers often talk about theirs as if they were pets.\n\nThe yeast and the bacteria do different jobs, and they work together in a kind of partnership. The yeast eats the simple sugars in the flour"},"finish_reason":"length","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":58,"completion_tokens":320,"total_tokens":378,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":48,"audio_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":171,"audio_tokens":0,"accepted_prediction_tokens":183,"rejected_prediction_tokens":0},"time_to_first_token_ms":222.059436,"response_token/s":31.64073636311758}}